>If it is a wand of wishing, why run the risk of the protection run?

Because the risk isn't as high as everyone thinks it is. Experienced
racketeers who aren't slavishly committed to XL1, low HP, underpowered pets,
and bad equipment can walk around the upper dungeon without too much fear.
When my monk hit Minetown he had 20 HP and an AC of -6 due to some nice +2
elven mithril. The armor also illustrates the production of the run too. +2
elven mithril is pretty useless to a working monk. It inhibits both fighting
and spellcasting. By doing the run I can replace that mithril with no impact
protection AC. It weighs nothing so I can carry more non-armor stuff. It has
no impact on spellcasting or fighting. It makes it trivially simple to get
the AC down into that essential negative range. I find the weight is a real
issue because armor, unlike most other items, is only useful to you if you
wear it. But by wearing it you can't do the same as other items and stick it
in a BoH greatly lightning the weight.

>Why not try to level up quickly so you can grab the eye quickly?

Because I want the AC flexibility too. Also you don't really need the Eye until
you get deeper in the dungeon. So there's no hurry to level up just for it.

